{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01TC", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-immersion-locally-quasi-finite}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6a97df0dfaebacdd8bfe59841b79448e7a48d003cc0d4921df99bc19ee452352", "source_text": "Any immersion is locally quasi-finite.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:35c014ade76408e0236109efe74fd247115683ce9053c1e16b1ac9ba9f2439a1", "unit_id": "tag:01TN:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01TC", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a3b66992757d919c3919b4c29604cbb92bbf3dd71f438393bc16530ad6602742", "source_text": "This is true because an open immersion is a local isomorphism\nand a closed immersion is clearly quasi-finite.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ee2fb735cb40cac97b1163da4bcfa16dd2ed3dca328da605659e45d0078edc9e", "unit_id": "tag:01TN:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01TC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0004": "$X \\to S$", "MATH_0005": "$x$", "MATH_0006": "$X \\to Y$", "MATH_0007": "$x$", "MATH_0008": "$X$", "MATH_0009": "$S$", "MATH_0010": "$X \\to Y$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-permanence-quasi-finite}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2876445a79f37ff8504e6792989a1fd64186a6cd31923dcfe93db145375fbac0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e03f2f45587517f36e2441ccc73b247af45779723eb5ad0924abb69d8578b58f", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes over a base scheme <MATH_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0003>. If <MATH_0004> is quasi-finite at <MATH_0005>, then\n<MATH_0006> is quasi-finite at <MATH_0007>.\nIf <MATH_0008> is locally quasi-finite over <MATH_0009>, then <MATH_0010>\nis locally quasi-finite.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:75c9ae09f5b80c167aa75b240a961dec5cec23702dd4bd8d7da837bfe118f3ca", "unit_id": "tag:03WR:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01TC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$A \\to B \\to C$", "MATH_0002": "$A \\to C$", "MATH_0003": "$B \\to C$", "MATH_0004": "$R = A$", "MATH_0005": "$S = S' = C$", "MATH_0006": "$R' = B$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-locally-quasi-finite-characterize}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-four-rings}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8128a71ba76fbd52e1efadfb1cb249dbc6670e3ae8a5751bdd1bfe4240fd384b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9142283826d01dbd52d5f2a5d4595b82dc65e8d1a78eaafcd72d90ffc2437b9d", "source_text": "Via Lemma <REF_0001> this translates\ninto the following algebra\nfact: Given ring maps <MATH_0001> such that <MATH_0002> is\nquasi-finite, then <MATH_0003> is quasi-finite.\nThis follows from\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0002>\nwith <MATH_0004>, <MATH_0005> and <MATH_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4e35fbbd68246789345e4dcbffe6a95bc52fd2325eefe1bb5b5eb70d3d21ace3", "unit_id": "tag:03WR:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01TC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$g : Y \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$g \\circ f$", "MATH_0005": "$g$", "MATH_0006": "$g : Y \\to S$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-quasi-finite-local-source}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d57d5c500affa7cdda218be08e1bfa019d202407be1783bcb2b28d4783bb2651", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d34d6cc9f8432fb83dab1ccc5db46a8117b85c56614aa79e149a51005a7932ed", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> be morphisms of schemes.\nIf <MATH_0003> is surjective, <MATH_0004> locally quasi-finite, and\n<MATH_0005> locally of finite type, then <MATH_0006>  is locally quasi-finite.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:37143e8da0ffd30aa24432579c282986dd51df6c2fbf947e571eac22ad91a14f", "unit_id": "tag:0GWS:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01TC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0002": "$y \\in Y$", "MATH_0003": "$s \\in S$", "MATH_0004": "$g \\circ f$", "MATH_0005": "$\\kappa(x)/\\kappa(s)$", "MATH_0006": "$\\kappa(y)/\\kappa(s)$", "MATH_0007": "$y$", "MATH_0008": "$Y_s$", "MATH_0009": "$f$", "MATH_0010": "$Y$", "MATH_0011": "$S$", "MATH_0012": "$g$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-residue-field-quasi-finite}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-algebraic-residue-field-extension-closed-point-fibre}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-quasi-finite-at-point-characterize}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9d746083c3173f793374bda9c20709f932bd870bbf3997f53357fca183c22a88", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:730c62aad608971186e60acd009ccf43211dfe97ef5df55228a5b45b7593538c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> with images <MATH_0002> and <MATH_0003>.\nSince <MATH_0004> is locally quasi-finite by\nLemma <REF_0001>\nthe extension <MATH_0005> is finite.\nHence <MATH_0006> is finite. Hence\n<MATH_0007> is a closed point of <MATH_0008> by\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nSince <MATH_0009> is surjective, we see that every point of <MATH_0010> is\nclosed in its fibre over <MATH_0011>. Thus by\nLemma <REF_0003>\nwe conclude that <MATH_0012> is quasi-finite at every point.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1a9457e914ed1892aa025953848bc58db11dba213ab34fdd175b15d1cd5c56c7", "unit_id": "tag:0GWS:proof"}
